wildos-shell (0.1.12) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Picking an accent colour no longer flashes a darker shadow round the
    windows, and with Blur windows in the background on, no longer makes
    the desktop darker with every pick. Windows now fade to their new
    colours through a Wild OS effect that mixes the old and new looks in
    one pass, in place of KWin's Blend Changes, which laid the old look
    over the new one so their shadows added up. The background blur also
    keeps its own drawing while any such fade runs, rather than blurring
    the fade's snapshot of its own work again.

