wildos-shell (0.1.10) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Three and four-finger swipes each have their own actions. The thumb
    and three finger pinches are gone: libinput drops a thumb that stays
    still and reports the rest as a three-finger swipe, so they only
    worked when the thumb moved too. Pinches of three or more fingers are
    still taken and do nothing.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:33:32 +0000

wildos-shell (0.1.9) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Touchpad gestures with three or four fingers that follow the fingers:
    swipe up for Task view, down to show the desktop, sideways to switch
    desktops, and a thumb and three fingers to pinch for all apps or spread
    for the desktop. Settings chooses the action for each and turns on
    three-finger drag. Win+D moves from the org.wildos.showdesktop script
    into the same KWin effect.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:33:25 +0000

wildos-shell (0.1.8) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Hot corners: each outer corner of the screen can open Task view, the
    windows of the app in use, the desktop, the app list, the notifications or
    a quick note, lock, turn the screen off, keep the computer awake or switch
    do not disturb, and can wait for a key to be held. Corners rest for a
    moment first, fire once per visit and stay quiet in full screen apps and
    games. A short note in the corner says when a switch went on or off.
  * The taskbar corner shows a cup while a hot corner keeps the computer
    awake; clicking it turns that off.
  * Start's app list and the notifications can be opened from outside the
    taskbar (org.wildos.Shell on plasmashell), for hot corners and touchpad
    gestures.

